  idea:"A person's rights are the whole shelf: some only a person should use, some left from old work. A role's rights come from its steps: each right names the step that needs it, and the steps only people do are left out.",
  points:["<b>A step needs it:</b> the planning agent's work reads it, writes it or calls it.","<b>Leave it out:</b> what only a person should do, and what's left from old work.","Work changes first, then rights follow: a new step, agreed, before a new right."],
  real:"Copying a person's rights to an agent is quick, and it hands it years of leftovers. Write the agent's steps first, then give one right per step, with the step's name beside it. Anything without a step stays off.",
